# =====================================================================
# Canonical authorized_keys — single source of truth
# =====================================================================
# Every `sync-keys.ps1` push REPLACES the remote ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
# with the exact contents of this file. To retire a key, delete its line
# here and re-sync; it disappears everywhere on the next push.
#
# Comment convention (3rd field on each key line):
#   <user>@<device-context>   e.g. jbusch@win-workstation
# Keep it human-readable — it's what you'll read when auditing drift.
#
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored by sshd.
# These are PUBLIC keys only. Never put a private key in this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

